            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <p>
                    Award-winning short film SKIN has just premiered on Vilpa Max. Coming in at just under 20 minutes,
                    the Academy Award-winning story explores the devastating consequences of a single, seemingly
                    innocent interaction between an African-American man and the son of a Neo-Nazi family.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The two groups first cross paths in a supermarket. Jaydee notices young Troy looking at a toy and
                    offers him a friendly smile. Troy's father, Jeffrey, misinterprets the gesture and confronts Jaydee,
                    turning a brief encounter into a deeply life-changing event. What follows sets both families on a
                    path that will have lasting consequences for everyone involved.
                </p>
                <p>
                    SKIN is a powerful and thought-provoking film that examines the enduring impact of racism and
                    prejudice, particularly in America. While the story presents an intense series of events, it serves
                    as a compelling reflection on hatred, intolerance, and the consequences they can have on individuals
                    and communities.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The film features an outstanding cast, including Jonathan Tucker as Jeffrey, Bashy as Jaydee, and
                    Jackson Robert Scott as Troy, best known for playing Georgie in the IT film franchise.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Viewer discretion is advised, as SKIN contains mature themes, scenes of violence, and the use of
                    racial slurs.
                </p>
                
